body:
> imo it makes it less readable.
> 
> > Many
> 
> So this means one or two?

Basically. Any code that increases indentation that can be changed to do the same thing with less indentation looks way cleaner. Indents make code especially with else's way harder to read, and the brackets at the end also add to the confusion.

example:

if (con1) {
if(con2) {
if(con3) {
return "d"
} else return "c"
} else return "b"
} else return "a"

will simplify to

if(!con1) return "a"
if(!con2) return "b"
if(!con3) return "c"
return "d"

which is a lot easier to understand.

